        <p>-likTOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next IN GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace for the COUN OF CHESTER will be held at the COURT HOUSE, NETHER KNUTSFORD. in and for the said County, on MONDAY, the 2nd day of April next, at half-past eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. when the Grand Jury will be empannelled. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Hun- dreds of Bueklow, Macclesfield, and Northwich, forming the Knutsford District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from such Hundreds, will take place at such Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Knutsferd District must be in attendance at the Court House, Knutsforcl, at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 2nd day of April next, at half-past eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE Court will be Adjourned to the Castle of Chester,. on THURSDAY,the sth day of April next, at eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Hundreds of Broxt,in, Eddisbury, Nantwich and Wirral, forming the Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last-mentioned Hundreds will take place at such Adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Chester District must be in attendance at the Castle of Chester, at the opening of the Court on THURSDAY, the sth day of April next, at eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester. Chester, 12th march, 1894. •</p>
