        <p>"0 V U M CLEMONT HOUSE, LITTLE SANGHOLL, NEAR CHESTER. 2nd Januar?, 1894. Mr. Jos. THORLEY. King's Cross, London. It may be of interest to you to know the follow- inv. On the 2nd October last, I purchasedl3 Hens and a Cock—all cross-bred—and a very miserable lot they looked ; in fact, they had been half famished. I gave them hot food in the morning—boiled potatoes and meal, with drip.Ong, bacon liquor, or such like stuff in it—and every other day about a teaspoonful of OVUM well mixed up. Result : up to prsent date, 2nd January, 513 eggs. Not a bad record, eh P especially seeing th It four were. old Hens. OVIM is GRAND Stuff. Yours truly, WM. CORFIELD. "0 VUM . " Is sold in Ca.=e.3 containing 72 Packets, 65., also in Bags-325., cwt. ; 16s. 6d., cwt.; Bs. 6d. Icwt. ; and 3s , Tib., carriage paid. JOSEPH THORLEY, KING'S CROSS, LONDON.</p>
